  "agent_type": "developer",
  "description": "Blocked reason: FINDING 1 (medium \u2014 violates AC \"No security anti-patterns around security-scoped URL handling\"): RecipesFolderStore.resolveBookmark() calls startAccessingSecurityScopedResource() on line 41 but never calls the matching stopAccessingSecurityScopedResource(). There is no deinit on RecipesFolderStore to balance this. Each call to RecipeDiscovery.scan() therefore executes two start calls against one stop, permanently leaking one reference count per app session. Fix: remove line 41 (`_ = url.startAccessingSecurityScopedResource()`) from resolveBookmark() \u2014 RecipeDiscovery.scan() is the correct place for start/stop per read, and it already does this correctly.\n\nRemaining work: Corrective bead needed: remove the orphaned startAccessingSecurityScopedResource() call from RecipesFolderStore.resolveBookmark(). The call on line 41 of RecipesFolderStore.swift starts security-scoped access but is never balanced by a stop \u2014 RecipeDiscovery.scan() already handles start/stop correctly per read, so this call is both redundant and leaking a reference count.",
